{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZrTWPFxb6Fbqt3XvvRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add an `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class. Initialize new orders to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed — the existing `save()` and `findById()` methods handle persistence and retrieval of updated order status.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt**: Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order (throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found, HTTP 404)\n   - If already CANCELLED, succeeds and returns the order unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Checks if any shipment is CONFIRMED (throws ConflictException if yes, HTTP 409, changes nothing)\n   - Changes order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Persists and returns the cancelled order\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add a `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the create method, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED (throws ConflictException if yes, HTTP 409).\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add new error code `ORDER_CANCELLED` for when a shipment creation is rejected because the order is cancelled.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an active order succeeds and returns order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling already cancels order is idempotent\n   - Cancelling with a CONFIRMED shipment rejects with 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate `OrderService` class: The ticket says not to add unrelated refactoring. The controller can handle the logic directly, as ShipmentController does. The existing code doesn't have service classes, so adding one would be scope creep.\n- Using an exception for the \"already cancelled\" case: I could throw a different exception, but the requirement explicitly says \"succeeds and changes nothing\", so HTTP 200 with the unchanged order is correct.\n- Adding error code `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED`: Not needed. The only failure case for cancellation is CONFIRMED shipment (409 CONFLICT).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | Order, Shipments by OrderId | Order.status=CANCELLED, CREATED Shipments.status=CANCELLED | Order (200 OK) | POST endpoint calls repo, updates entities, saves |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED order | Order | Nothing | Order (200 OK) | POST endpoint returns order unchanged |\n| Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment | Order, Shipments by OrderId | Nothing | 409 CONFLICT, code ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED | POST endpoint throws ConflictException before any writes |\n| Cancel non-existent order | (none) | (none) | 404 NOT_FOUND, code ORDER_NOT_FOUND | POST endpoint throws ResourceNotFoundException |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | Order, Shipment | (none) | 409 CONFLICT, code ORDER_CANCELLED | POST /shipments checks order status, throws ConflictException |\n| Create shipment for non-existent order | (none) | (none) | Creates shipment (no validation today) | Current behavior unchanged |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order**: Create an order, cancel it, verify it returns 200, order status is CANCELLED, and the order can be fetched with CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **Cancel already cancelled**: Cancel an order twice, verify second call returns 200 and nothing changes.\n\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment**: Create order and shipment, manually mark shipment as CONFIRMED, try to cancel, verify 409 CONFLICT with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED code, and verify order/shipment states unchanged.\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order**: POST cancel for non-existent ID, verify 404 NOT_FOUND with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code.\n\n5. **Cancel CREATED shipment**: Create order and shipment, cancel order, verify shipment status is now CANCELLED.\n\n6. **Create shipment for cancelled order**: Create and cancel order, try to create shipment for it, verify 409 CONFLICT with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n7. **Existing tests still pass**: Verify all existing order and shipment tests continue to work (they should, since we initialize orders to ACTIVE and don't break the shipment contract).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":21412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8712996a-dd65-4d5a-b93c-b3b6471ecec5","uuid":"d6058d0f-44aa-40fa-93b2-25c880119b48","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:23:18.351Z","request_id":"req_011CfZrTW1RwJo1eMep8CJG5"}
